  "fullDescription": "Moonweek is an interactive weekly planner that runs in your browser — on your computer and on iPad. It’s not a PDF or a spreadsheet: drag tasks between days, check off subtasks, and watch your week’s progress grow as a moon, a mountain or a tide.\n\nWhat’s included:\n\nMoonweek_EN.html — desktop version in English\n\nMoonweek.html — desktop version in Russian\n\nLinks to the iPad versions (English and Russian)\n\nIllustrated user guide (PDF, English and Russian)\n\n**Plan your week: **\n\nAdd tasks to any day and sort them by color-coded categories (create your own)\n\nBreak big tasks into subtasks — a progress bar shows how far along each task is\n\nLong-running tasks carry over from day to day until they’re done\n\nMark a task “not needed” — it won’t spoil your stats\n\nAdd notes for every day\n\nFlexible like your week – drag tasks to another day, reorder them, or send them to next week\n\nHold Ctrl/Cmd while dragging to copy a task\n\nUndo and redo any change (Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y)\n\nSee your progress – progress rings for every day: done, planned, total\n\nWeek progress as a moon, a mountain or a tide — with a little celebration at 100%\n\nSuccess streak and weekly analytics by day and category\n\nMake it yours – 23 themes: soft pastels, bright colors, high-contrast and seasonal themes with background art\n\nNight mode for calm evenings\n\nSave, print and back up – download your week as a PNG image or a print-ready A4 PDF\n\nBack up all your tasks to a small file and restore them anytime\n\nMove your tasks between computer and iPad with the same backup file On iPad. Add Moonweek to your Home Screen — it opens like an app. Tap, hold and drag with your finger; two-finger tap to undo How it works Download the file and open it in your browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari).\n\nNo installation, no sign-up, no subscription. The desktop version works offline. Your tasks are stored privately in your browser on your device.\n\nPlease make a backup once a week (one click). Requirements – Computer: a recent version of Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari – iPad: Safari on iPadOS 15.4 or later.\n\nNot designed for phones. Please don’t share or resell the files or the iPad links.",
